    "measurementTechnique": [
      "All collected samples were filtered through 0.2um Sterivex filters and analyzed for dissolved organic carbon (DOC), total dissolved nitrogen (TDN), absorbance and fluorescence spectroscopy, and ultra-high resolution mass spectrometry. Water depth and salinity were measured using EXO and SonTek sensors deployed adjacent to the surface water sampling equipment. DOC and TDN concentrations were determined by Shimadzu TOC-L equipped with a TNM-L unit. Absorbance and fluorescence were collected using Horiba Aqualog. For ultra-high resolution mass spectrometry, samples were acidified to pH 2 with HCl and extracted by passing through PPL cartridges. MeOH extracts were re-constituted to DOC concentration of 80 mg/L in MeOH/ACN (80/20 v/v%) and analyzed on Thermo Vanquish UHPLC coupled with an Orbitrap Exploris 240. Obtained mass spectra were processed using the CoreMS data analysis framework. Full methodological details are provided in \u201cVariations in the optical and molecular composition of dissolved organic matter from coastal wetlands\u201d by Kim et al. (submitted)."
    ],
